  "id": "cat-cry-syndrome",
  "term": "cat-cry syndrome",
  "definition": "Cat-cry syndrome is a genetic infant disorder caused by deletion of the short arm of chromosome 5. It is marked by a distinctive cat-like cry along with poor growth, small head size, intellectual disability, muscle stiffness with weakness in all four limbs, and characteristic facial and genital differences.",
